  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IHE Desalination training in Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Because of its scarce water resources, Egypt operates 125 desalination plants. Its government is in development of a strategic plan to further increase this capacity. The complexity of desalination technologies requires specialised knowledge and technical expertise in various fields, including water chemistry, plant maintenance &amp; energy efficiency, and advanced desalination methods e.g. reverse osmosis. This training program is aiming at the enhancing of the capabilities of personnel working in desalination plants and equip them with the skills necessary to handle the unique challenges of operating desalination systems, ensuring the sustainability of this vital resource.</narrative>
  </description>
